Performance Testing
1. Testing Objective

The objective of testing is to verify that the ACL configuration correctly enforces the required access permissions.

2. READ Testing

Verify that authorized users can view permitted records and unauthorized access is restricted.

3. CREATE Testing

Verify that only users with the required CREATE permission can create records.

4. WRITE Testing

Verify that only authorized users can modify existing records.

5. DELETE Testing

Verify that only authorized users can delete records.

6. Unauthorized Access Testing

Attempt access using users without the required permissions and verify that access is denied.

7. Administrator Testing

Verify that administrators can access and manage all required records.

8. Testing Result

The testing process verifies that the configured ACL rules enforce the intended access restrictions for the Institution Details table.
